        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "The incubation of peripheral-blood lymphocytes with a lymphokine, interleukin-2, generates lymphoid cells that can lyse fresh, noncultured, natural-killer-cell-resistant tumor cells but not normal cells. We term these cells lymphokine-activated killer (LAK) cells.",
