        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Your sentences should usually begin with elements that are relatively short, simple (not simplistic), and direct: perhaps a short introductory phrase or clause, followed by a short, concrete subject, followed by a verb expressing a specific action. After the verb, the sentence can go on for several lines if it is well constructed (see Lessons 9 and 10). The general principle is to carry the reader not from complexity to simplicity but from simplicity to complexity.",
            "block_bbox": [
                114,
                903,
                771,
                1046
            ],
            "block_id": 16,
            "block_order": 15,
            "group_id": 16,
